<%# crosswire:contract v1 %>
<%#
  Deliberately dumb. `input.tag_name` picks `:textarea` or `:input` — everything
  else (size class, type, invalid, loading) lives in Crosswire::UI::Input, so this
  file is safe to restyle, shadow, or eject. See docs/DECISIONS.md D6.

  A `<textarea>` has no `value` attribute — its content IS the value, so the ONE
  conditional below chooses between `content_tag` (textarea, value as content) and
  `tag` (input, a void element — `input.attrs` already carries `value` as a real
  attribute when multiline is false, see Crosswire::UI::Input#element_attrs).

  Locals:
    input  Crosswire::UI::Input
%>
<% if input.multiline %>
  <%= content_tag(:textarea, input.attrs) { input.value } %>
<% else %>
  <%= tag("input", input.attrs) %>
<% end %>
